Delayed branching can help in the handling of control hazards
The following code is to run on a pipelined
processor with one branch delay slot:
I_{1}: ADD R_{2} ← R_{7} + R_{8}
I_{2}: SUB R_{4} ← R_{5} - R_{6}
I_{3}: ADD R_{1} ← R_{2} + R_{3}
I_{4}: STORE Memory [R_{4}] ← R_{1}
BRANCH to Label if R_{1} == 0
Which of the instructions I_{1}, I_{2}, I_{3} or I_{4} can legitimately occupy the delay slot without any other program modification?
